From 9628de7656ee36d23a0c5f1cc26aa6cf17a31ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zelda3-ds <zelda3-ds@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:36:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] rgds: multi-language support with runtime language selection

- i18n.c: languages compiled into zelda3_assets.dat (kDialogueMap) plus
  interface texts from lang/<code>.ini next to the executable.
- The dialogue language can change at runtime; a message already on screen
  keeps the encoding and font it was built with (messaging.c).
- Translated pause menu (item names, ability words, box headers) built from
  the HUD letter tiles (hud.c).
- Translated file select screens: text rows of the ROM tilemaps and of the
  select_file.c stripe tables are rewritten with the 8x16 font (nmi.c,
  select_file.c).
- Bottom screen: every text goes through I18n_Get, UTF-8 accented capitals
  are drawn with diacritics, and a LANGUAGE row in the settings cycles the
  available languages and saves Language in zelda3.ini.
